      {
        "id": 93440,
        "name": "Katsue",
        "username": "Katsue",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/{size}/2012_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-03T23:07:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"JimmytheRat\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/c37758/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> JimmytheRat:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We have a houserule that targets that have some sort of retaliation won't hit themselves with it.&nbsp; Gauntlets of Perdition will still activate, but Backlash Field, Flame Barrier, Combat Stance, the Chairman, etc. don't.Not strictly official, but it makes a lot more sense than Wraith punching herself in the gut every round because she's got the Sewer Flu.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Looking at some of the known symptoms of Sewer Flu, which include punching yourself already (see Afflicted Frenzy), I can easily believe she'd start punching herself.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:19:39.884Z",
